{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MolecularConstruction.PalindromicityOrbitalType","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MolecularConstruction.PalindromicityOrbitalType","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.instPalindromicityOrbitalTypeOfNatNat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.instPalindromicityOrbitalTypeOfNatNat","kind":"instance","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L82-L92","doc":"Z=2 instance: helium is palindromic and Z ≤ 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType.palindromic_iff_s_type","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType.palindromic_iff_s_type","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The histogram is palindromic iff all occupied sub-shells are s-type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType.histogram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType.histogram","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The NF histogram at atomic number Z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType.mk","kind":"ctor","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.PalindromicityOrbitalType","kind":"class","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L68-L80","doc":"**Conjecture.** For the quotient atom model in H_{Z+1}(q), the\nword-length histogram is palindromic for Z ≤ 4 (pure s-shells)\nand non-palindromic for Z ≥ 5 (p-shell occupied).\n\nThis is the Poincaré duality statement: palindromicity holds\nwhen the NF occupies a self-dual sub-lattice of the Bruhat\norder on S_{Z+1}, which happens precisely for s-type orbitals. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:palindromicity-orbital-type","label":"conj:palindromicity-orbital-type","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.helium_histogram_palindromic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.helium_histogram_palindromic","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L54-L64","doc":"The helium histogram is [0, 1, 1, 0] — zero terms at length 0,\none at length 1 (σ₁), one at length 2 (σ₀σ₁), zero at length 3.\nThis is palindromic (Poincaré dual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.h3_histogram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.h3_histogram","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L32-L50","doc":"The word-length histogram of an H₃(q) NF element.\n\nBasis elements by word length:\n- Length 0: 𝟏 (slot 0)\n- Length 1: σ₀, σ₁ (slots 1, 2)\n- Length 2: σ₀σ₁, σ₁σ₀ (slots 3, 4)\n- Length 3: σ₀σ₁σ₀ (slot 5)\n\nThe histogram counts nonzero coefficients at each length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.IsPalindromic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.IsPalindromic","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/palindromicity-orbital-type.lean#L26-L29","doc":"A sequence of natural numbers is palindromic if it reads the same\nforwards and backwards. ","signatureChunk":0}]}